{"title":"Root mean cube","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The root mean cube of a set of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffe3184d129c91ece11f40d326ab67a53ad11e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x_1, x_2, x_3,\\cdots,x_a]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> is defined as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95ba192352b5c0ee7e7fc7fda60f1cf343076642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x_1^3+x_2^3+x_3^3+\\cdots+x_a^3}{a}}\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Mentioned in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=RMS-AM-GM-HM\" title=\"RMS-AM-GM-HM\">RMS-AM-GM-HM</a>. Also, in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_Mean_Inequality\" title=\"Power Mean Inequality\">Power Mean Inequality</a>, where the exponent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is 3.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Root_mean_cube&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105558\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 16/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 568/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.521      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.521      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24106:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018